{"event": "token", "client_s": 10.651, "data": {"request_id": "127a29dfad86", "seq": 29, "ts": "2026-10-28T03:18:33.805Z", "t_ms": 10649, "delta": " token, `Retrieve`, at the beginning of each output segment given the prompt $x$ and previous generation $y_{<t}$"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 10.918, "data": {"request_id": "127a29dfad86", "seq": 30, "ts": "2026-10-28T03:18:34.072Z", "t_ms": 10916, "delta": " [C1, C2, C3, C7]. The decision is handled in one of two ways during inference:\n\n* **"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 11.099, "data": {"request_id": "127a29dfad86", "seq": 31, "ts": "2026-10-28T03:18:34.253Z", "t_ms": 11097, "delta": "Hard Control (Discrete Token Prediction):** The model decodes a `Retrieve` token directly from its vocabulary [C2, C"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 11.291, "data": {"request_id": "127a29dfad86", "seq": 32, "ts": "2026-10-28T03:18:34.445Z", "t_ms": 11289, "delta": "3]. If it predicts `Retrieve == Yes`, the external retriever is called to fetch passages; if it predicts `Retrieve =="}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 11.518, "data": {"request_id": "127a29dfad86", "seq": 33, "ts": "2026-10-28T03:18:34.671Z", "t_ms": 11516, "delta": " No`, retrieval is skipped, and the model continues generating standard text [C2, C3]. The token can also take a `continue"}}
